-- title:
--   Chart ring of a flat varpi-adic tower with G-action
-- statement:
--   Let $S$ be a commutative ring and $\varpi \in S$ an element that is a non-zero-divisor, i.e. $\varpi s = 0$ implies $s = 0$. Let $X'_n$ be schemes with morphisms $xb'_n : X'_n \to \operatorname{Spec}(S/(\varpi^{n+1}))$ and transition morphisms $xt'_n : X'_n \to X'_{n+1}$, and assume that for every $n$ the square formed by $xt'_n$, $xb'_n$, $xb'_{n+1}$ and the morphism $\operatorname{Spec}(S/(\varpi^{n+1})) \to \operatorname{Spec}(S/(\varpi^{n+2}))$ induced by the quotient map attached to the inclusion $(\varpi^{n+2}) \subseteq (\varpi^{n+1})$ is a pullback square, and that each $xb'_n$ is flat. Let $G$ be a finite group acting at each level by group homomorphisms $a'_n : G \to \operatorname{Aut}(X'_n)$, with each automorphism commuting with $xb'_n$ and with the transitions, i.e. $a'_n(g)$ followed by $xt'_n$ equals $xt'_n$ followed by $a'_{n+1}(g)$. Let $W'_n \subseteq X'_n$ be open subschemes, each affine, with $xt'_n{}^{-1}(W'_{n+1}) = W'_n$ and $a'_n(g)^{-1}(W'_n) = W'_n$ for all $g$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a commutative ring $R'$ carrying an $S$-algebra structure and an action of $G$ by ring automorphisms commuting with the $S$-scalars, such that $R'$ is adically complete for the ideal generated by the image $\varpi$ of $\varpi$ in $R'$, such that this image is a non-zero-divisor on $R'$, and such that there are ring isomorphisms $\mathrm{lvl}'_n : R'/(\varpi^{n+1}) \xrightarrow{\sim} \Gamma(X'_n, W'_n)$ satisfying three compatibilities: restriction along $xt'_n$ from $W'_{n+1}$ to $W'_n$ carries $\mathrm{lvl}'_{n+1}(x)$ to $\mathrm{lvl}'_n(x)$ for every $x \in R'$; pullback of sections along $a'_n(g^{-1})$ on $W'_n$ carries $\mathrm{lvl}'_n(x)$ to $\mathrm{lvl}'_n(g \cdot x)$; and, for $s \in S$, $\mathrm{lvl}'_n$ sends the class of the image of $s$ to the pullback along $xb'_n$, from the whole of $\operatorname{Spec}(S/(\varpi^{n+1}))$ to $W'_n$, of the global section corresponding to the class of $s$ under the isomorphism $\Gamma \circ \operatorname{Spec} \cong \mathrm{id}$ for the ring $S/(\varpi^{n+1})$.
--
--   This is the construction of the chart ring of a compatible chain of $G$-stable affine opens in a flat $\varpi$-adic tower of schemes: the inverse limit of the section rings $\Gamma(X'_n, W'_n)$ is a $\varpi$-adically complete, $\varpi$-torsion-free $S$-algebra with $G$-action whose successive quotients recover the levels. Phrased purely in Mathlib terms, it is used by [`AlgebraicGeometry.TowerQuotientDatum.exists_ringEquiv_fixedPoints_quotient_basicOpen_of_isPullback_of_flat`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.TowerQuotientDatum.exists_ringEquiv_fixedPoints_quotient_basicOpen_of_isPullback_of_flat) to produce rings of invariants on quotients of such towers.
-- source:
